{"name":"Flannel","hex":"#9e917c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flannel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft cloth material originally woven from wool, today often combined with cotton or synthetic fibers.","A washcloth."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of flannel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flannel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flannel","blocks":[{"text":"Flannel is a soft woven fabric of varying fineness. Flannel was originally made from carded wool or worsted yarn, but is now often made from either wool, cotton, or synthetic fiber. Flannel is commonly used to make tartan clothing, blankets, bed sheets, sleepwear, and several other uses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Flannel_Shirt_For_Abi.jpg/330px-Flannel_Shirt_For_Abi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flannel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg/500px-Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg/1280px-Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg/500px-Washer_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red flannel skirt, designed by Sybil Connolly in 1957","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWasher_Woman_skirt_1957_by_Sybil_Connolly.jpg"}],"sounds":{"flannel":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/En-au-flannel.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&u